@page "/"

<PageTitle>AI-Assisted Support Routing</PageTitle>

<div class="landing">
    <section class="hero">
        <h1>AI-Assisted Support Routing</h1>
        <p class="hero-subtitle">Messages classified and routed in real time via Azure Service Bus</p>
    </section>

    <section class="pipeline">
        <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-box">Customer Message</div>
            <p class="pipeline-desc">Customer sends a support request</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-box">AI Classifier</div>
            <p class="pipeline-desc">System classifies by content</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="pipeline-step">
            <div class="pipeline-box">Department Inbox</div>
            <p class="pipeline-desc">Routed to the right team in real time</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="send-message">Send a Message</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg" href="departments">View Departments</a>
    </section>

    <section class="how-it-works">
        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>
            .NET Aspire orchestrates three workers communicating via Azure Service Bus topics.
            When a message arrives, the Classifier worker analyses the content and publishes a
            classified message to the next topic. The Handler worker picks it up, generates a
            response, and pushes the result to the Departments view in real time.
        </p>
        <p>
            The classifier sits behind an IMessageClassifier interface, and the implementation is
            chosen from configuration rather than from code: a keyword matcher (the default, and what
            the tests run), a local model through Ollama (what F5 runs), or OpenAI. Model answers fall
            back to the keyword matcher on a bad reply, a timeout or an error, so nothing outside the
            declared categories is ever published. Every hop is traced end-to-end via OpenTelemetry,
            including the model call, and visible in the Aspire dashboard.
        </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="tech-stack">
        .NET 10 &middot; Aspire 13.6.1 &middot; Azure Service Bus (emulator locally) &middot; Blazor Server &middot; OpenTelemetry
    </footer>
</div>

<style>
    .landing {
        max-width: 48rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem 1rem;
    }

    .hero {
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .hero-subtitle {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: #6c757d;
        margin: 0;
    }

    .pipeline {
        display: flex;
        align-items: flex-start;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 0;
        margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .pipeline-step {
        text-align: center;
        flex: 0 1 10rem;
    }

    .pipeline-box {
        border: 2px solid #0d6efd;
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        background: #f8f9fa;
        color: #212529;
    }

    .pipeline-desc {
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        color: #6c757d;
        margin-top: 0.4rem;
    }

    .pipeline-arrow {
        flex: 0 0 2.5rem;
        align-self: center;
        height: 2px;
        background: #adb5bd;
        position: relative;
        margin-top: -1.2rem;
    }

    .pipeline-arrow::after {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        right: -1px;
        top: -4px;
        border: 5px solid transparent;
        border-left: 7px solid #adb5bd;
    }

    .landing-actions {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .how-it-works {
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .how-it-works h2 {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .how-it-works p {
        color: #495057;
        line-height: 1.7;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .tech-stack {
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        color: #adb5bd;
        padding-top: 1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid #eef0f2;
    }

    @@media (max-width: 640px) {
        .pipeline {
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0;
        }

        .pipeline-arrow {
            width: 2px;
            height: 1.5rem;
            margin-top: 0;
        }

        .pipeline-arrow::after {
            right: -4px;
            top: auto;
            bottom: -1px;
            border: 5px solid transparent;
            border-top: 7px solid #adb5bd;
            border-left: 5px solid transparent;
        }

        .hero h1 {
            font-size: 1.5rem;
        }
    }
</style>
